DAY 37 - PART B: LAB
Watch the controllers and scheduler work
Time: 75-90 minutes
==================================================================

STEP 1: Watch the chain of controllers
--------------------------------------
Terminal 2:
  k get events -w --field-selector involvedObject.namespace=default

Terminal 1:
  k create deploy chain --image=nginx:1.27 --replicas=2

Events appear in this order:
  ScalingReplicaSet (deployment-controller)
  SuccessfulCreate  (replicaset-controller)
  Scheduled         (default-scheduler)
  Pulling/Pulled/Created/Started (kubelet)

Write down which component reported each.


STEP 2: Owner references and cascading delete
---------------------------------------------
P=$(k get pod -l app=chain -o name | head -1)
k get $P -o jsonpath='{.metadata.ownerReferences[0].kind}/{.metadata.ownerReferences[0].name}{"\n"}'
RS=$(k get rs -l app=chain -o name)
k get $RS -o jsonpath='{.metadata.ownerReferences[0].kind}/{.metadata.ownerReferences[0].name}{"\n"}'

k delete deploy chain --cascade=orphan
k get rs,pods -l app=chain       # still there, now ownerless
k delete $RS                     # pods removed by GC


STEP 3: Read the controller manager and scheduler logs
------------------------------------------------------
k logs -n kube-system kube-controller-manager-lab-control-plane --tail=20
k create deploy logs-demo --image=nginx:1.27 --replicas=3
k logs -n kube-system kube-controller-manager-lab-control-plane --tail=20 | grep -i logs-demo
k logs -n kube-system kube-scheduler-lab-control-plane --tail=20
k delete deploy logs-demo


STEP 4: Stop the scheduler and see what breaks
----------------------------------------------
docker exec lab-control-plane mv /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-scheduler.yaml /root/
sleep 15
k get pods -n kube-system | grep scheduler       # gone

k create deploy nosched --image=nginx:1.27 --replicas=2
k get pods -l app=nosched -o wide                # Pending, NODE <none>
k get rs -l app=nosched                          # RS created pods fine

Controllers still work; only placement stopped.

Bring it back:
  docker exec lab-control-plane mv /root/kube-scheduler.yaml /etc/kubernetes/manifests/
  sleep 20 ; k get pods -l app=nosched -o wide   # now scheduled


STEP 5: Schedule by hand (be the scheduler)
-------------------------------------------
vi manual.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: manual
spec:
  nodeName: lab-worker2
  containers:
  - name: c
    image: nginx:1.27
k apply -f manual.yaml ; k get pod manual -o wide
nodeName set = scheduler skipped entirely.


STEP 6: Stop the controller manager
-----------------------------------
docker exec lab-control-plane mv /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-controller-manager.yaml /root/
sleep 15
k scale deploy nosched --replicas=4
k get deploy nosched ; k get pods -l app=nosched   # still 2! No one acts
k delete pod -l app=nosched                         # deleted, not replaced
docker exec lab-control-plane mv /root/kube-controller-manager.yaml /etc/kubernetes/manifests/
sleep 30 ; k get pods -l app=nosched                # reconciles to 4

Level-triggered: it didn't need to "see" the events it missed; it
compared desired and actual when it came back.


STEP 7: Simulate a node failure
-------------------------------
k scale deploy nosched --replicas=6
k get pods -l app=nosched -o wide
docker stop lab-worker2
k get nodes -w            # ~40 s: NotReady
k describe node lab-worker2 | grep Taints
k get pods -l app=nosched -o wide -w
After ~5 minutes the pods on lab-worker2 go Terminating and new ones
start on lab-worker. Note the timestamps.
docker start lab-worker2
k get nodes               # Ready again


